#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/review-log-watch.bpmn:80
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "For each changed row, the agent pass of Contributor feedback on a working draft: Ready for agent = Yes gets its edit, Ready for merge = Yes its merge, and a Blue answer to a Decision needed question is taken up. Every new row (from an issue, a person or a TWG workbook), every row with an empty Feedback (agent) and every row whose Blue cells changed gets feedback in the same wake (owner, 2026-11-01: \"agent should provide feedback whenever blue change or whenever new row added\"), in the fixed layout: the ask first (Decision needed: with lettered options, one recommended, and where to answer), then Proposed direction: and Next:, only the tags bold (Q-FBK-1 A). The agent then runs tools/review-log-watch/lint.ts and fixes what it flags: a cell that breaks the layout, or a PR state that GitHub contradicts. The agent records its step on the Agent tab at once, with the real time."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/review-log-watch.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "For each row in the tool's append list (one per issue that no row's Issue cell links yet; owner, Q-WATCH2 B), appends it below the last row of Contributor Feedback: Title is the issue's title, the first Contributor Feedback column @login (#N): the issue's first paragraph, Issue its URL. The script gives each new row its Change-set id. No other writer adds issue rows. Then each row linking a closed issue (the tool's closedRows, and the rows just appended as closed) is hidden and its text struck through (owner, 2026-11-01 10:18Z)."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/review-log-watch.bpmn:36
